ceived_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Armynator/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-05T11:47:56Z","updated_at":"2025-04-05T11:55:29Z","body":"I ran into this issue with the PhysicsServer3D.BodyCreate() function. https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99307 solved it for me.\n\n> Do you have any real world examples where this many objects would actually be reasonable? The limit is 262144 total allocated RIDs, which is pretty huge.\n\nIn my case I'm loading all objects in the world as static colliders on a dedicated server. When bypassing the Node system, it only takes around 600mb of RAM for 1 million static colliders. IMO that's reasonable and something I'd expect a general purpose game engine to handle just fine. Modern physics engines (Jolt, PhysX 4+, Box2D 3.0, Bepu) support ridiculous amounts of static colliders for exactly this usecase, so having an artificial limit on something simple like RIDs seems weird to me.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2780679899/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2794583703","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104176#issuecomment-2794583703","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104176","id":2794583703,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6mkfaX","user":{"login":"Zapathie","id":32038102,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMDM4MTAy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32038102?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zapathie","html_url":"https://github.com/Zapathie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zapathie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zapathie/following{/other_user}","gists_u